[0.009, "o", "PyChess on macOS\r\n================\r\n\r\nPyChess is a GTK3 / PyGObject desktop application. It runs on macOS using the\r\nGTK libraries provided by Homebrew.\r\n\r\nTested with: macOS 14 (Sonoma) and later, Apple Silicon\r\n             (see .github/workflows/macos-build.yml).\r\n             Intel Macs use the same steps, with /usr/local wherever Apple\r\n             Silicon uses /opt/homebrew. CI also checks the Intel gettext/libintl\r\n             lookup; the full GTK build job runs on Apple Silicon.\r\n\r\n\r\nQuick install (recommended)\r\n---------------------------\r\n\r\nIf you just want to install PyChess and get a normal double-clickable app, use\r\nthe bundled installer. From inside a PyChess source checkout run:\r\n\r\n    ./macos/install.sh\r\n\r\nThis single command installs the Homebrew GTK stack, builds a virtual\r\nenvironment that re-uses Homebrew's PyGObject, installs PyChess, and produces a\r\nself-contained `PyChess.app` in your `~/Applications` folder that you can launch\r\nfrom Launchpad or Finder. See `macos/install.sh` for wha"]
[0.000, "o", "t it does step by step.\r\n\r\nThe rest of this document describes the manual steps the installer performs, in\r\ncase you prefer to install by hand or need to debug a problem.\r\n\r\n\r\n1. Install the binary dependencies with Homebrew\r\n------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nIf you do not have Homebrew yet, install it from https://brew.sh.\r\n\r\nThen install the GTK stack and supporting libraries:\r\n\r\n    brew install python gtk+3 pygobject3 gtksourceview4 librsvg \\\r\n                 gstreamer adwaita-icon-theme gettext stockfish\r\n\r\n- `python`            : the Homebrew Python. PyGObject is built against it, so the\r\n                        macOS system Python cannot be used.\r\n- `gtk+3`             : the GTK 3 toolkit.\r\n- `pygobject3`        : Python bindings for GTK and other GObject libraries.\r\n- `gtksourceview4`    : syntax-highlighted move/PGN views.\r\n- `librsvg`           : renders SVG board and piece themes.\r\n- `gstreamer`         : sound support, including the GStreamer Python bindings.\r\n- `adwaita-icon-th"]
[0.000, "o", "eme`: required so PyChess can show its icons.\r\n- `gettext`           : provides `msgfmt`, used to compile translations at build\r\n                        time, and libintl at runtime. Homebrew keeps gettext\r\n                        keg-only, so PyChess also checks its `opt/gettext` path.\r\n- `stockfish`         : the chess engine used for analysis and play.\r\n\r\nMake sure the Homebrew `bin` directory comes before `/usr/bin` in your PATH:\r\n\r\n    export PATH=\"$(brew --prefix)/bin:$PATH\"\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Create a virtual environment and install the Python dependencies\r\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nHomebrew's Python is marked as externally managed (PEP 668), so `pip install`\r\nrefuses to write into it and fails with \"error: externally-managed-environment\".\r\nCreate a virtual environment that can still see Homebrew's PyGObject:\r\n\r\n    cd <repository root>\r\n    python3 -m venv --system-site-packages .venv\r\n    source .venv/bin/activate\r\n    python -m pip install --upgrade pip\r\n    python "]
[0.000, "o", "-m pip install -r requirements.txt\r\n\r\n`--system-site-packages` is what lets the virtual environment use Homebrew's\r\n`gi` module instead of trying (and usually failing) to build PyGObject from\r\nsource.\r\n\r\nRun the remaining steps with the virtual environment activated.\r\n\r\n\r\n3. Generate the locally-built data files (first checkout only)\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nBefore running or installing, generate the opening-book database and the piece\r\ntheme previews. These are not shipped in the repository:\r\n\r\n    PYTHONPATH=lib python3 pgn2ecodb.py\r\n    PYTHONPATH=lib python3 create_theme_preview.py\r\n\r\nBoth commands need `PYTHONPATH=lib`, because they import pychess from the source\r\ntree rather than from an installed copy.\r\n\r\n\r\n4. Run PyChess from the source tree\r\n-----------------------------------\r\n\r\n    python3 pychess\r\n\r\nIf icons are missing, or you see GSettings schema errors, make sure the Homebrew\r\nshare directory is on XDG_DATA_DIRS:\r\n\r\n    export XDG_DATA_DIRS=\"$(brew --pr"]
[0.000, "o", "efix)/share:$XDG_DATA_DIRS\"\r\n    python3 pychess\r\n\r\nA ready-made launcher that detects the Homebrew prefix, exports all the required\r\nenvironment variables for you and picks up `.venv` automatically is provided at\r\n`macos/run.sh`:\r\n\r\n    ./macos/run.sh\r\n\r\n\r\n5. Install it properly (optional)\r\n---------------------------------\r\n\r\nWith the virtual environment activated:\r\n\r\n    pip install .          # regular install\r\n    # or, for a development install:\r\n    pip install -e .\r\n\r\nThis installs the `pychess` console script, so afterwards you can start PyChess\r\nwith just:\r\n\r\n    pychess\r\n\r\nThe data files are installed under `<prefix>/share/pychess` and are found\r\nautomatically at runtime.\r\n\r\n\r\n6. Chess engine\r\n---------------\r\n\r\n`pychess` looks for a chess engine for analysis and play. The `stockfish`\r\nformula installed in step 1 is auto-detected when it is on your PATH; otherwise\r\npoint PyChess at it explicitly via Preferences -> Engines.\r\n\r\n\r\nTroubleshooting\r\n---------------\r\n\r\n- \"error: externally-managed-enviro"]
[0.000, "o", "nment\"\r\n      You are running `pip install` against Homebrew's Python directly. Create\r\n      and activate the virtual environment from step 2 first.\r\n\r\n- \"ImportError: cannot import name Gtk\" / \"Namespace Gtk not available\"\r\n      You are using the macOS system Python, which cannot see Homebrew's\r\n      PyGObject. Use the Homebrew Python: `brew install python`, then re-run with\r\n      `/opt/homebrew/bin/python3` (Apple Silicon) or `/usr/local/bin/python3`\r\n      (Intel).\r\n\r\n- \"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pychess'\"\r\n      The script imports pychess from the source tree, so it needs\r\n      `PYTHONPATH=lib` (see step 3).\r\n\r\n- No icons / missing application icon\r\n      Install `adwaita-icon-theme` and ensure the Homebrew share directory is on\r\n      XDG_DATA_DIRS (see step 4).\r\n\r\n- \"WARNING: libintl not found\" at startup\r\n      Install gettext: `brew install gettext`. PyChess still starts without it;\r\n      what you lose is translations.\r\n\r\n- No sound\r\n      Make sure GStreamer is installed:\r\n      `br"]
[0.000, "o", "ew install gstreamer`.\r\n"]
